Comments: [Evaluator: Christian Iliadis; Date: 11/20/2024]
1. Er = 410 keV: resonance energy from the reported excitation energy in Caggiano et al. (2001); proton partial width from the C2S value of the 23Ne mirror state;
   gamma-ray partial width from the shell-model result reported in Wiescher et al. (1988); the latter is in approximate agreement when correcting the experimental
   lifetime of the 23Ne mirror state for the large difference in the gamma-ray decay energy.
2. Er = 1335, 1633 keV: proton partial widths from the C2S values of the 23Ne mirror states; the gamma-ray partial widths are a guess based on the measured lifetime
   values of the 23Ne mirror states; our assignment of Ex(23Al) = 1773 keV to Ex(23Ne) = 2315 keV (5/2+) is plausible, but not unambiguous.
3. The direct capture S factor for the ground state is estimated using the experimental spectroscopic factor of the 23Ne mirror state [C2S = 0.24; Endt 1977].
